.TH CW "1" "October 2026" "cw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cw \- cw join
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cw
\fI\,join \/\fR[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,NAME \/\fR[\fI\,TARGET\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
Add a window to an existing Context.
.IP
NAME can include \fI\,/WindowName\/\fP to set the window's name in the Context. TARGET
can be a ref number or an iTerm window title. If TARGET is omitted, adds the
current (focused) window.
.IP
Examples:
.TP
cw join MyProject
add current window
.TP
cw join MyProject/Dev
add current window, name it "Dev"
.TP
cw join MyProject 3
add window by ref number
.TP
cw join MyProject IoT
add window by iTerm title
.TP
cw join MyProject/Dev IoT
add IoT window, name it "Dev"
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-window\-name\fR TEXT
Name for this window within the Context.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this message and exit.
